! conclusion: 
  verify that FUTON3 exports (trails, pattern drafts) land in Arxana nodes, that GravPad pads reference current prototypes, and that editor workflows can replay a proof state without manual rescue

  + context: Verify that all outputs from FUTON3 are correctly integrated into workflows to maintain the tranquility of the system.

  + IF:
    FUTON4 provides a tranquil atelier (Arxana + graph memory + GravPad) that cools and integrates the proofwork

  + HOWEVER:
    tranquility evaporates when proof trails aren’t ingested or when GravPad lacks synced pads

  + THEN:
    verify that FUTON3 exports (trails, pattern drafts) land in Arxana nodes, that GravPad pads reference current prototypes, and that editor workflows can replay a proof state without manual rescue

  + BECAUSE:
    passaddhi keeps the system from running hot; this layer must prove it can settle the energy from F3/F2

